# Attribution and license boundaries

The original Python code and project documentation are MIT licensed, copyright
2026 Bhagyesh Kamal. The project was developed with AI coding assistance;
independent validation and numerical limitations are documented in the reports.

Our generated arrays, numerical tables and plots are licensed under
[Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Attribute Bhagyesh Kamal and this repository. Where a comparison uses author
data, also attribute the dataset below and the paper. Generated curves and
overlays are independent calculations, not the authors' original figure files.

## Original scientific work

Saikat Guha, Tiju Cherian John, Zihao Gong and Prithwish Basu,
*Quantum-enhanced quickest change detection of transmission loss*,
[arXiv:2503.12276v2](https://arxiv.org/html/2503.12276v2).
The physical models and paper results are credited to these authors. This
repository is independent and implies no endorsement. Manuscript PDF/TeX and
original paper figure files are not redistributed; no rights to them are asserted.

## Imported author dataset

Saikat Guha and Prithwish Basu (2025), *Dataset accompanying PRL publication on
quantum-enhanced quickest change detection of transmission loss*, v1,
Zenodo, [DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17460928](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17460928).
License: CC BY 4.0, as recorded in the preserved Zenodo API metadata.

`data/zenodo_17460928/prl_fig3_data`, `prl_fig7_data`,
`prl_supplem_fig4b_data` and `plot_PRL_figs.m` retain their original bytes and
published checksums. The plotting script is parsed/read as source material and
is not executed by the Python implementation. `data/zenodo_17460928/README.md`
and `manifest.json` provide full provenance. These files are not MIT relicensed.

The release archives contain our simulation arrays. Historical summaries and
notebook outputs are labeled as original study snapshots where appropriate;
their dates and limitations must be retained when quoting them.
